    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_89d7664f79a55b22c9d9e005c2283e7ff2ad88d1646ed06803f3786714b0fd0e",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The decomposition mΔ⁺(x)=JΔ(Δx) plus a squared-sinc term separates a zero-integral odd component from the component carrying the entire L1 excess. Absolute integrability and oddness annihilate the integrals of JΔ(Δx) and f, leaving the explicit correction mass π/(2Δ); independently, exponential type and integrability give Fourier support in [-Δ,Δ] by Paley-Wiener, and the pointwise envelope gives the uniform transform bound. These conclusions require the stated parity, integrability, type, and envelope and do not re-prove one-sided order.",
      "parent_sources": [
