    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_871ed19cf5a20ea468e28e7fe9596b8942347268eee0f72609d1465dbf3d27db",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The even and odd problems share a transfer pattern: represent the target kernel by a finite nonnegative Gaussian-subordination measure, invoke the corresponding solved Gaussian extremal theorem, dilate the resulting majorant and minorant to bandwidth Δ, and compute the directional L1 cost from the resulting construction. This common mechanism connects representation, one-sided order, scaling, and quantitative error across the two otherwise separate sections.",
