    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_971e933f2d9f30a0b3e90ba8f5056878003f55a1b5a1d0fbf12a006fca02175e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The odd Gaussian-subordination construction depends on three logically separate certificates: the proposed measure must reproduce HΔ, its density must be nonnegative, and its total mass must be finite. The main construction invokes all three conditions, and the appendix discharges them respectively by integral transformations, a monotonicity certificate, and monotone convergence; together they make the cited odd extremal theorem applicable rather than merely furnishing ancillary calculations.",
